From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: bound monitor descriptor poll work

The monitor loop debits its budget only at a valid end of PPDU, yet returns
all consumed descriptors as NAPI work. Empty, invalid, flushed and partial
PPDU entries can therefore run beyond the advertised poll weight and delay
other data queues. Charge every descriptor once; the existing continuation
state keeps partial PPDU parsing across polls.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_mon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_mon.c
@@ -3283,6 +3283,7 @@ ath12k_wifi7_dp_mon_srng_process(struct
 		spin_unlock_bh(&buf_ring->idr_lock);
 
 		if (unlikely(!skb)) {
+
 			ath12k_warn(ab, "monitor destination with invalid buf_id %d\n",
 				    buf_id);
 			goto move_next;
@@ -3305,17 +3306,12 @@ ath12k_wifi7_dp_mon_srng_process(struct
 			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_DATA,
 				   "Monitor dest descriptor end reason %d", end_reason);
 			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
+
 			goto move_next;
 		}
 
-		/* Calculate the budget when the ring descriptor with the
-		 * HAL_MON_END_OF_PPDU to ensure that one PPDU worth of data is always
-		 * reaped. This helps to efficiently utilize the NAPI budget.
-		 */
-		if (end_reason == HAL_MON_END_OF_PPDU) {
-			*budget -= 1;
+		if (end_reason == HAL_MON_END_OF_PPDU)
 			rxcb->is_end_of_ppdu = true;
-		}
 
 		end_offset = u32_get_bits(info0, HAL_MON_DEST_INFO0_END_OFFSET);
 		if (likely(end_offset <= DP_RX_BUFFER_SIZE)) {
@@ -3330,6 +3326,10 @@ ath12k_wifi7_dp_mon_srng_process(struct
 		__skb_queue_tail(&skb_list, skb);
 
 move_next:
+		/* Bound all ring work, including empty and discarded descriptors.
+		 * ppdu_continuation below preserves partial PPDU parsing across polls.
+		 */
+		*budget -= 1;
 		ath12k_dp_mon_buf_replenish(ab, buf_ring, 1);
 		ath12k_hal_srng_dst_get_next_entry(ab, srng);
 		num_buffs_reaped++;
